From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:38:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-sm8250: enable the parent PLL while
 configuring the pixel clocks

On SM8150 (Surface Duo) every boot warns twice during display probe:

  disp_cc_mdss_pclk0_clk_src: rcg didn't update its configuration.
  disp_cc_mdss_pclk1_clk_src: rcg didn't update its configuration.

The pixel clock sources are reconfigured while their parent, the DSI PHY
PLL, is not running yet, so the RCG never latches the new configuration.
Set CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE on both, as the qcm2290, sm6115, sm6350, sm6375,
sm7150 and sm8750 display clock controllers already do.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the
direction of Bryson, who tested it on his Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
index 8f433e1e7..d021cf2f2 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
@@ -578,7 +578,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 disp_cc_mdss_pclk0_clk_src = {
 		.name = "disp_cc_mdss_pclk0_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_6,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_6),
-		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
 		.ops = &clk_pixel_ops,
 	},
 };
@@ -592,7 +592,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 disp_cc_mdss_pclk1_clk_src = {
 		.name = "disp_cc_mdss_pclk1_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_6,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_6),
-		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
 		.ops = &clk_pixel_ops,
 	},
 };
